{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_07e_what_the_handler_produces", "label": "07e-what-the-handler-produces.md", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "page", "source_file": "docs/java/pages/phase-11-testing/06-mockmvc/07e-what-the-handler-produces.md", "source_location": "L1", "frontmatter": {"title": "@ResponseStatus on an exception class and a bare ResponseStatusException are resolved by a DIFFERENT resolver that also calls sendError, so under MockMvc they produce exactly the empty-bodied response a bare @Valid failure does \u2014 and the handler&#x27;s return type decides the rest, where a String on a plain @ControllerAdvice is a VIEW NAME and a DTO with no status is a 200 carrying an error", "sidebar_label": "07e \u00b7 What the handler produces", "sidebar_position": "21"}, "_origin": "ast"}, {"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_07e_what_the_handler_produces_responsestatus_on_the_exception_class_a_different_resolver_the_same_empty_body", "label": "`@ResponseStatus` on the exception class: a different resolver, the same empty body", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/java/pages/phase-11-testing/06-mockmvc/07e-what-the-handler-produces.md", "source_location": "L33", "_origin": "ast"}, {"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_07e_what_the_handler_produces_responsestatusexception_and_the_hierarchy_that_decides_whether_it_has_a_body", "label": "`ResponseStatusException`, and the hierarchy that decides whether it has a body", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "heading", "source_file": "docs/java/pages/phase-11-testing/06-mockmvc/07e-what-the-handler-produces.md", "source_location": "L79", "_origin": "ast"}, {"id": "docs_java_pages_phase_11_testing_06_mockmvc_07e_what_the_handler_produces_controlleradvice_versus_restcontrolleradvice_the_view_name_trap", "label": "`@ControllerAdvice` versus `@RestControllerAdvice`: the view-name trap", "file_type": "document", "node_kind": "head